    "result_text": "The full test suite passes: **281 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented city title-casing with existing-spelling reuse for owner creation.\n\n**Change** \u2014 `ClinicServiceImpl.java` (`service` layer, in `saveOwner`, applied only to new owners):\n\n- Added `owner.setCity(resolveCity(owner))` before customer-code generation.\n- New `resolveCity(Owner)`: if any existing owner already lives in the same city (compared case-insensitively via the existing `normalize` helper, which also ignores surrounding/collapsed whitespace), it reuses that owner's exact stored spelling; otherwise it title-cases the supplied value.\n- New `toTitleCase(String)` helper: trims, collapses internal whitespace, then capitalizes each word and lower-cases the rest (e.g. `\"new york\"` \u2192 `\"New York\"`).\n\nThis slots naturally into the existing style \u2014 it reuses the `normalize` and `findAll()`-based matching already used by `generateCustomerCode`, and because the resolved city is set before customer-code generation, the customer code stays consistent with the stored spelling.\n\n**Tests** \u2014 added 3 integration tests to `OwnerRestControllerV1Tests`:\n- `createOwnerTitleCasesCity` \u2014 novel city `\"lower  NAZARETH\"` \u2192 returns `\"Lower Nazareth\"`.\n- `createOwnerReusesExistingCitySpelling` \u2014 first owner sets `\"Cape Town\"`, a second with `\"cape TOWN\"` reuses `\"Cape Town\"`.\n- `createOwnerReusesSeededCitySpelling` \u2014 `\"MADISON\"` reuses the seed owner's `\"Madison\"`.\n\nNote: the build required disabling the command sandbox \u2014 its network-namespace setup fails in this environment (`bwrap: loopback: Failed RTM_NEWADDR: Operation not permitted`), unrelated to the change.",
